## Continuation update (2026-09-26; oneway initiation and outbound hook order)

- Compared Java `invokeOneway`, `invokeAsync`, `invokeImpl` against the Rust client. Rust `invoke_oneway` was an async method: dropping its unpolled future performed no work, unlike Java's immediate `getAndCreateChannelAsync` initiation. Converted it to a synchronous starter returning a ready result future; it immediately submits the transport task to the client-owned task registry, and dropping the result future does not cancel transmission. It still does not await admission/write, and Tokio may not poll/connect before method return, so strict initiation timing and Java's synchronous connect/admission/send errors remain different.
- Moved async callback outbound `before_request` hooks to after connection acquisition and before semaphore admission, matching Java's `invokeAsync` -> `invokeImpl` order. Moved the sync/future hook before admission likewise; GO_AWAY retry still skips duplicate before hooks. Added `p3_outbound_rpc_hook_runs_before_async_admission_wait`; amended the oneway test to drop the returned future and verify the peer receives the frame later.
- Updated ADR and compatibility inventory/matrix; corrected statements to avoid claiming Tokio starts polling/connection before return. Inventory explicitly marks sync/future/oneway hook ordering as code-reviewed but only callback path currently has a dedicated admission-order regression test. Reconfirmed Java inbound processor/hook branches, callback order and GO_AWAY implementation from pinned source. Rust TLS encrypted-key parser has no password/decryption support; no insecure or global reload API added.
- Validation PASS: `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-remoting --locked --offline` (10 unit + 4 codec + 46 transport, doc tests); `cargo test --workspace --locked --offline` (11 common + 9 protocol + 1 protocol fixture + 10 remoting unit + 4 codec + 46 transport, doc tests); `cargo fmt --all --check`; `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked --offline -- -D warnings`; `python3 scripts/check-workspace-metadata.py`; `python3 tests/differential/compare.py --self-test`; `git diff --check`.
- English and Traditional Chinese Phase 3 plans reread in full. P3-V01/V02/V03/U01 remain locally covered; Java full-parity acceptance remains blocked by observable Netty/API/executor/error/TLS/oneway/scan differences and unclosed exhaustive ledger. Phase 3 NOT ACCEPTED; Phase 4 prohibited; P3-V04 stays for Phase 19. No Maven/live Broker/Docker run; Java checkout untouched.
- Added `p3_outbound_rpc_hook_runs_before_sync_admission_wait` after review found that only the callback-path hook ordering had a regression test; the shared future/sync path is now directly covered.
